Run m4's own test suite (checks/) but not gnulib's self-tests (tests/).

gnulib's tests hang in the build chroot right after test-error.sh, holding
the worker until its timeout, although every m4 test passes. They exercise
the vendored portability layer, not m4. The top-level SUBDIRS is
". examples lib src doc checks po tests"; the override runs everything but
tests (a command-line SUBDIRS reaches the sub-makes too, none of which uses
the variable).

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -48,3 +48,3 @@
 check() {
 	cd "$pkgname"
-	make check
+	make check SUBDIRS='. examples lib src doc checks po'
 }
